ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1003 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1004,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1005,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1006,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1007,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_271,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_527,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_584,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_752,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_999 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7380e800ff652bdbd5a8127cb1563305"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "We can't practice awareness of speech alone; we have to speak to somebody. We have to pay attention to an outside object, not just our own mind and body, so we lose mindfulness because our attention goes fully outside and then we are no longer attentive internally or to our speech. We start to think about the other person and look at the other person and then all our attention and our awareness goes outwards and our attention is no longer also directed toward ourselves. On the other hand, practicing talking meditation too formally and only in paying attention to one self will make the conversation stiff and unnatural."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1008 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1009,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1010,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1011,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1012,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1013,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1014,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_247,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_49,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_560,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_86,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_988 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e8effc35b37352ace56c100ad3da741e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "A yogi said in a Finnish retreat that while the retreat is quite good for mindfulness, there's a lot of stuff happening and especially in speaking. When speaking with others, a yogi has to be responsive and quick and it feels like they're doing two jobs at once. Yes--it will be this way. It's all about skill, and skill is gained from continued practice. We will be slow in any subject when we are not skillful as yet. As we do it over and over again, we gain momentum and the process becomes easier. While there may be a lot of personal effort in the beginning, it eventually begins to roll on its own momentum, like riding a bike. I liken it to martial arts, where at first you are practicing some simple moves and after a while (you don't know when), you can just use them automatically. In this same way, the mind may now be a little slow and deliberate when it begins this practice, but as you keep doing it, you will find it slowly becoming automatic."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1015 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1016,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1017,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_15,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_167,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_214,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_341,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_584,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_588 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "be7301af35626aac0a6eb9296d1d0987"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "You could try practicing in this way: Know what you want to say. Think about what you want to say before you say it. When you acknowledge to yourself first, to what you feel and think before you speak, you are giving yourself time to know yourself before you speak. Try this over and over again. You can be aware of your experience as you are listening to the other person and recognize that you are listening. You are listening and knowing and are aware that you are listening and they are listening and then you are aware that the act of listening is happening, that speech is happening."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1018 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1017,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1019,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1020,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1021,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_481,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_588,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_86,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_996 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3b690d21b677c7cdedf155fd00446719"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "You might have to practice this quite actively; it will be difficult at first but only because you haven't had enough practice. Every new thing you learn is difficult when it is new because you don't have enough practice. When your overall mindfulness becomes more natural and continuous and has some momentum through practice and you know the mind and recognize it at work, it becomes easier to notice when you are talking. You will notice when the mind is thinking, when it is listening, when it is hearing, looking, and so on. You will need to accept that at first you will lose mindfulness quite a lot. Just don't give up."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1022 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1023,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1024,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1025,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1026,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1027,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_229,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_247,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_349,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_463,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_948 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1f5469bbdb6ee5c53403bde292b7af2d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "Before I learned how to practice in social situations, I would spend as much time as I could by myself and did concentration practice. The mental stability was there but I couldn't find peace because I was resistant to social situations. I wasn't skillful but tried over and over again. As I learned to practice with people around, slowly over a long time, the mind's habit changed; my awareness increased and slowly became automatic. When I saw that my resistance was because of conditioning, I actively set out to practice in social situations to overcome the resistance."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1028 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1006,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1029,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1030,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_195,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_394,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_395,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_932 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a5e0bffc238120e2d4ee12194c985bb0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "At one point, I decided to practice right speech, meaning no lying, no harsh speech, no slander, and no idle talk. Taking on this task really helped me in talking meditation because I had to check if I was doing any of the four wrong speeches. It reduced the amount of talking tremendously and my practice just shot up because we speak so often and I had to be so mindful all the time."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1031 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1032,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1033,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_507,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_569,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_712 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c3f94e58e32985feccf30b371c241fd0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "I don't remember how long I practiced actively like this but after some time of practicing I could maintain my peacefulness while I was with others. After I was more settled, I actively increased the practice and sought out places that disturbed me because I knew that's where my weakness was. I would go to those places and keep trying there. Sometimes I would walk into a bar and meditate. I wanted to know how much this affected my mind and I became really interested. Everyone around me was drunk and talking loudly but I was very peaceful. This is how I developed confidence in my practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1034 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_988 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "506f66d0980f8cd5f3f3579001688372"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "It's good to know, as information, that, it is possible to be mindful when you speak. Then you are willing to try and put this aspect of mindfulness practice into your daily life, to challenge yourself to use this as part of your practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1035 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_527,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_584,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_614,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_752,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_988 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SPEAKING MINDFULLY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a6b65951ac4486dcaf4c9c1a25b1e9c7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 13 ;
    neo:text "It is very easy for defilements to come into our speech when we speak about ourselves, when the \"I\" becomes involved. At home we usually speak without mindfulness and it is this habit, rather than mindfulness, that tends to come in when we speak. When we are speaking, there are three things we can be mindful of: our mind, our speech and our body. If we know our mind then we should definitely be able to filter that into knowing our speech and our body as well."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1036 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1037,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1038,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1039,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1040,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1041,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_229,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_246,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_311,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_995,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_996 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "SEEING IS DIFFERENT FROM LOOKING"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e5a0b2d76e98c1921bf1891ab19a4279"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "You need to have your eyes open while meditating in daily life. I learned how to be aware with my eyes open because fellow shopkeepers used to tease me when I meditated at work with my eyes closed. They thought I was sleeping on the job! So I learned to pay attention to the internal landscape while keeping my eyes open. I eventually became more skillful at knowing the difference between seeing and looking, and the people I worked with didn't even know that I was meditating."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1042 a neo:Document ;
