    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "35c00e852fd122613fa9c0b6b3fd7f58"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "We encounter this all the time. In Western society, people wait in a queue or line because there is a belief that people should wait their turn for something. There is a dissonance when someone cuts that queue/line and thoughts that they should be in line start coming up. Or different thoughts of fairness might come up. There could be another kind of belief, \"I wanted to get to my food and she has slowed that down by jumping the queue.\" The mind has convinced itself of all these strands of thought! At times like these, we should ask ourselves, \"What internal belief is being thwarted here?\" Right now, someone's actions are frustrating these beliefs and the mind justifies this anger against the other person!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1126 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1127,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1128,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1129,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1130,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1131,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1132,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_210,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_463,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_619,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "STRINGING EACH OTHER ALONG"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f04e3ba8e56411e146a944a0dec7a39b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "In daily life, we give each other compliments and thank each other for their compliments. We string each other along by reinforcing the need to look good and feel good. If instead we had said, \"You look really terrible,\" the listener might get irritated because people want to feel good. We are often at the mercy of other people's words, compliments or insults and are generally automatically affected. When there is an understanding of how these thoughts work in the background, the wanting will disappear."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1133 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1073,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1134,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1135,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1136,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1137,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1138,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1139,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1140,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1141,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_31,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_529,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_600,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_803,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_804,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_964 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9cd9a28644f164ffd7f6c076453a5b6e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "It is very important that there is a right attitude when we are working in the world. Sometimes we may feel like we are being taken advantage of or being taken for granted. How different would it be if we thought these people were acting in a certain way because they didn't know any better? If someone were bullying you, it would be really tough to handle! You may get tense, agitated or angry with the bully. What if you thought that this person was only inadvertently doing these things because she didn't know better? How would you feel then? You can better understand and forgive. SELF-JUDGMENTS \"Bad\" is just a label. Don't label yourself that. When the mind is wholesome, the person is good and when the mind is unwholesome, the person is bad. It's only for that moment and that's always changing. Continue to practice and take your time; the fact that you are practicing shows that your mind wants to become better and that means that the mind will become better."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1142 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1143,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1144,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_210,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_224,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_271,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_359,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_972 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b03e7db145de7391c39b00dbcac02b2f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When doubt is strong in the mind, do not pay attention to these thoughts. Once we give attention to these kinds of thoughts, they suck us in and grow. We can anchor ourselves to feelings instead and not give any power to the conceptual thinking. Follow the same principle for other strong, unwholesome states. When we look at the feeling and discontinue looking at the thoughts, it will help the mind calm down. Then we can look at these thoughts and feelings together when we feel we're ready."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1145 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1146,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1147,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_366,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_446,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_67,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_800 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "86c020c903f2a99bf0be76a13ba201f6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Everyone has his or her own path and there's a natural course that needs to unfold for each person. You can watch what's happening in the mind and understand it, but you can't force it. You may learn a technique at a retreat, but it is when you go home that you can apply that technique all the time. That's when your life changes."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1148 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1149,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1150,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1151,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1152,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_293,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_317,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_318,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_366,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_382,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_914 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "PRECONCEPTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "261694bb8ac27232b5585ebb73848a52"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "How do you experience silence? How do you experience the stillness of a garden or the woods? I've asked different people this question. Fear comes up for some people. Youngsters tell me that they get bored when there's nothing to occupy them. As you can see, good or bad depends on the person experiencing it, depending on their preconceived feelings of it."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1153 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1154,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1155,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1156,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1157,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_587 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "PRECONCEPTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "436f3e8deeb643754bc31af1f3d13cfe"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "There are tons of these accumulations that you have from childhood and you really want to see these ideas that have built up over the years. If these little preconceptions are seen properly, then the mind will no longer be disturbed by what is happening. If you continue to meditate regularly, there ought to be fewer and fewer attachments."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1158 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1037,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1096,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1097,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1159,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1160,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1161,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_289,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_463 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GIVING COMES IN DIFFERENT WAYS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "692445517f6d93256d01857a7f7eab75"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The market where I had my shop was a very busy place. Lots of shops were lined up side by side with narrow alleys between them. Shopkeepers sent goods in and out with carriers who ran back and forth for the shopkeepers. People would run quite blindly, not caring who was in the way. I would get irritated whenever I had to get out of the way, which was quite often! I knew that people would run into me if I didn't move aside, but also became annoyed that I was the one who always had to be careful. This was a daily occurrence."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1162 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_111,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1131,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1163,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1164,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1165,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1166,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1167,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1168,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1169,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_165,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_366,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_463 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GIVING COMES IN DIFFERENT WAYS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "18a8aa1e56fd7f3334d2bdd080b8ee1d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When I began to practice continuously, I became mindful of my irritation with this market situation. After being mindful of it regularly for a long time, I actually began to see it as a good practice to give space to these people to prevent accidents and I saw moving aside as a practice of generosity. As I practiced day after day and mindfulness arose, good actions also followed. The aversion that accompanied the critical mind decreased. With aversion gone, I began to feel metta for these people."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1170 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_214,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_790,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_877,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "715f307d8e38bf022192e42fda594003"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "In daily life, where wisdom may be weak, you want initially to pay attention to awareness. The mind can recognize the situation happening while awareness naturally collects data in the background. As awareness picks up more data from the experience, and the picture becomes complete and wholesome minds grow stronger, you will eventually stop acting out of defilements."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1171 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1172,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1173,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1174,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1175,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1176,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_208,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_86,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_877,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "72bf6cf8ee3d7c1094e1994eccb0ada9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Let's say you are in a social situation and you have accidentally said something harsh because there was too much momentum to speak. Let awareness continue to know in the background while you're talking to others. At some point of seeing this whole process, awareness will have enough of a picture that wisdom can arise and resolve the situation. It is inevitable to make some wrong turns in daily life but you have to learn how to profit from these experiences. Don't allow defilements to run freely or your situation will deteriorate."^^xsd:string .

