        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_251,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_34,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_466,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Continuing the Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GATHERING MOMENTUM, COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "79bdbd82fb160e2851bc9caeeabc8722"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "I want you to use your wisdom to continue the work. You collect this gold dust a bit more each day, day by day. You learn from it all while this and that goes on in your lives. Mindfulness is a lifetime commitment, not a part-time job. It is something that you really, really need to do all the time. All the time. Only when you see the nature of the mind will you understand the nature of dhamma. The mind is just arising and passing away, is so ephemeral, and the only input you can have to this process is the quality of awareness. When awareness becomes natural, it means that you have been putting in the effort to keep it going: persistence is right effort. Awareness starts staying. Effort remains and it becomes much more natural and much more useful."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1359 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1360,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1361,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1362,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_201,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_955 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Continuing the Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GATHERING MOMENTUM, COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "91b2b077306e31ad21293944a63a6961"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Vipassana wisdom cannot come about through intellectual thinking. It simply cannot be comprehended. Vipassana insight is not something that can be conceptualized through images; it is a wholly new understanding and insight into principles, into nature."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1363 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1364,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1365,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1366,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Continuing the Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GATHERING MOMENTUM, COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e832bfb69aca4357d8a850149cee65b5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "As we practice diligently and continuously, we will keep having these small understandings and insights over and over. Over the long haul, insights will become so persistent that they will work in tandem with awareness. Once wisdom starts working together with awareness, our meditation moves to a higher level of understanding. We begin to have bigger insights."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1367 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_251,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Continuing the Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GATHERING MOMENTUM, COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "35b6196599104d91a5a090d11b7724c5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "These bigger understandings have a life of their own; they have more power. They are not so dependent anymore on awareness. Once we have had such insights, they will always be available and wisdom will always be there. At this stage, awareness will step back to play a secondary role. It will always be present because wisdom cannot exist without awareness, but at this level of understanding, wisdom begins to have a life of its own. Awareness will keep feeding wisdom and our understandings will grow in strength. At this stage, the mind always knows what to do, and it can happen that the practice becomes so easy that it will keep going even if we are not making any effort to practice. The more we practice, the more the mind understands how to practice and it doesn't have to think about how to practice. It finds its way when wisdom starts to operate."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1368 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1369,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_34,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_759 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Continuing the Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GATHERING MOMENTUM, COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "030717352fd3b88aa7c334a840a6d2c1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "The real benefit of the Dhamma is not to stop engaging with life issues but to approach the same tasks with wisdom instead of defilements, having understood how they work."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1370 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1371,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1372 ;
