        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Appendix: Mindfulness in Brief"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aa5a4c93325f42319baef017c0fcde8a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "For example, if I am sitting on a rug right now and I'm aware of this rug, this is not considered meditation awareness. When I am aware of the process of seeing or feeling that allows me to see and feel and interpret this rug as a rug, this is my experience. I am aware of this experience. Being aware of only the conceptual part of the experience is not sati. We are not as interested in the concept of a rug in-as-much as we are in the process of seeing or feeling. We need concepts in order to function in daily life, but in meditation we want to know the underlying process of what is happening in the mind, of nature, and of reality."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1412 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1209,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1413,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_251,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_554,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_608,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_68 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Appendix: Mindfulness in Brief"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "23da7c6347cd6f73b9360bba971ec74c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "So you are aware and you maintain that awareness. You do not have to use much energy to be aware. There's no need to focus hard but you do need to use right effort to keep reminding yourself to go continuously. If you can use energy in that right way, you can go on practicing the whole day without feeling tired. Try to sustain that awareness for longer periods of time throughout the day."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1414 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1415,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1416,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_177,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_210,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_359,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_770 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Appendix: Mindfulness in Brief"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "18efe2d758af5cc09e94d7148986b81f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "You can take one object that you know lightly and use that as a grounding object to explore more widely. When I was practicing continuously in daily life, I would use feeling as my touchstone. From there I began to notice how thoughts affected feelings and how feelings affected thoughts. I slowly learned and understood all these relationships."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1417 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1418,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1419,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1420,
