        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_43,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_44,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Acknowledgements"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e6695110d38fa524eb92f164533a2828"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "I want to express my appreciation to all yogis. Their questions and difficulties have once again inspired many of the explanations in this book. I really hope that this book will help yogis better understand mindfulness meditation and deepen their practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_381 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_239,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_271,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_354,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_379,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_382,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_383,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_384,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_385,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_386,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_387,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e2b542578d74dae5c7f291706b945830"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 24 ;
    neo:text "And these accumulated practices of collecting the mind enabled me to then be more aware of the interactions within my own mind when I was making decisions, counting money or attending to customers. I could notice when I lost my composure and devise a plan for maintaining it in my next interaction, always using the practice of collecting the mind as the basis for strengthening the mind's composure. As these interactions happened daily and routinely, this is how I learned what helped me to maintain the composure of my mind, what helped me to remain aware and maintain continuity--when I needed to pick up attention on one object, mainly when I was no longer interacting with someone else or doing a task and when I needed to be aware in a more fluid way as in when customers approached and I had to attend to them and interact with them. The awareness became closer to continuous and insights naturally arose more and more over time."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_388 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_195,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_267,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_389,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_390,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_391,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_392,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_393,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_394,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_395,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_396,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_397,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_398 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "25facbf8b0298b9f224bacb3dcb603a0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 25 ;
    neo:text "A year in, I read an article about the ajivatthamaka sila, eight precepts with right livelihood as the eighth precept. I was particularly interested in the expansion of the precept on not telling untruths, into four precepts for right speech: refraining from telling lies, slander, harsh speech, and idle chatter. I was inspired to try this. The depression had already made me quite subdued at the marketplace I worked at, compared to the joker I had been previously, and then practicing continuously made me quieter."^^xsd:string .

