        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "74629ecb2ddc2988510b8328d080ac73"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 26 ;
    neo:text "However, taking on the four right speech precepts left me with hardly anything to say because I now avoided idle chatter. If someone came over to gossip about some other stallholder, they no longer found in me someone that sympathized. I merely listened and did not contribute as I saw neither wisdom nor meaning in adding fuel to their fire. The mindfulness became so much keener, aware of everything I said or planned to say and naturally the strength and composure of the mind also improved."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_406 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_300,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_384,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_407,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_408,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_409,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_410,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_411,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_412,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_413 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b909400e04580f36cac34f181de989c2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 27 ;
    neo:text "After two years of practicing dedicatedly I began to notice that I had been avoiding unnecessary interactions and I began to challenge myself to go to social functions as a representative of my family and maintain mindfulness, or to go out for dinner with old friends and maintain my mindfulness, composure, or my stand without frustration or rudeness when they tried to get me to join them in drinking alcohol. I even went for a boxing match and learned a lasting lesson that this was not the place for me any longer."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_414 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_247,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_415,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_416,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_417,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_418,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_419,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_85 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9a334930013d22894b69a9026ba36067"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 28 ;
    neo:text "I tell you this story to say this is possible for you as well. You just have to persevere, experiment, and use your wisdom to figure out what works until this also becomes a natural part of your life. I want to persuade you that this is possible. I really want you to know that you can do it at home when you have become skillful in this practice. This is my motivation to continue teaching. The only reason we aren't able to bring it into our lives is because we don't know enough yet or aren't practicing enough yet."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_420 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_311,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_348,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_366,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_39,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_421,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_422,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_423,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_424,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_67,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_68,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "cfe0821bce0561e996870c438cec62ab"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 29 ;
    neo:text "You may go on formal retreats to develop wholesome minds. But it is very important that you continue meditating outside of retreats because unwholesome minds arise in the absence of wholesome minds. Right now, as soon as yogis leave a retreat, they have no idea where all the wholesome minds have disappeared! It seems as if wholesome minds just arise on retreat, only to be replaced by unwholesome mind states as soon as a person returns home. You have to cultivate your own energy and your own wisdom. If you are suffering, you will need to sit down and work out what to do about it. If the parents always work things out for the child, the child will never learn for himself."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_425 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_426,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_427,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_428,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_429,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_430,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_431,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6edd243b7499591bad0b2c6cb3620798"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 30 ;
    neo:text "Finally, we all have to live, but we must ask ourselves: Are we truly alive? If we don't change and grow, it is akin to being dead. I encourage all of you to please continue practicing. I make an aspiration for all of you to practice at home and to enjoy the fruits of your practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_432 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_39,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_433,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_434,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_435,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ae9f8e0ebb5bdaa867aeb12ecc3b82d4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 31 ;
    neo:text "When I know the mind is aware, there is a very strong feeling of goodness. I greatly wish for yogis to understand and appreciate fully the value of awareness + wisdom and their role in helping develop all of the wholesome qualities of the mind. This is the basic understanding that will carry the rest of the practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_436 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_112,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_49,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_67 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "dcad7165cd01e3c42a5e5eee548d0d27"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "When a retreat begins, defilements will negotiate with the yogi: \"Okay, how long do you want to practice for? One month? Two months? Three months? All right. We'll leave you alone for that long. But when the retreat is over, then it's our turn again!\" And it really is their turn again. Delusion loves hearing the line, \"The retreat is over!\" It is very common to think that we've finished meditating. When this happens, it is now time for defilements to come back out to play."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_438 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_218,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_221,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_250,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_439,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_440,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_96 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2859dcc8229ec21dacd16a292c416f09"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When I was younger, I went for long retreats of six to ten months at a time. My mind cleared up while I was in retreat but I stopped practicing back home and my mind went back to square one. My life did not change. I never listened to my teacher's advice to continue practicing at home and got into deep trouble! It was only when I was in the deepest trouble that I saw the need to work it out in daily life. I began to practice continuously at home and realized the need to meditate all the time."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_441 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_103,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_256,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_442,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_443,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_444,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_445,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_446,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "52f4b26f892e3939d98e1a93e1eb1b6d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "When you return home, remember that you are there, at home. You should remain in the present moment there. The present moment is the only real thing. Stay where you are because the now is always now, there is no \"after now.\" You're trying to have mindfulness in this mind and the only effort is to remember to be mindful in the present moment. Through everything in your life you are remembering to be mindful, remembering how to be mindful, and building and maintaining samadhi, or stability of the mind."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_447 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_239,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_448,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_449,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_450,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_451,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_452 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1dc56b3d85cc9ba986cb58bde502dafd"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "You use the information that you have, combined with intelligence, logic, and reasoning to figure out how to practice correctly. Next, you learn how to keep these already developed insights alive. Finally, you figure out how to develop even deeper levels of insight."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_453 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_204,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_256,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_34,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_454,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_455,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_456,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_457,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_458,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e16d8ed1b4470f7b207885b02208ffc5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "We must be walking on the Noble Eightfold Path of sila (moral conduct), samadhi (stability of mind), and panna (wisdom). This particular aspect of meditation, where you need to be practicing it all the time for it to be alive and beneficial becomes apparent to someone who practices continuously. We really need to be a close friend of the Dhamma in order to grow in the Dhamma. It is when we are in such close communion with the Dhamma that we can grow in it. Otherwise, there is not much growth. How can the Dhamma grow in us if we are not always living the Dhamma?"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_459 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_112,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_34,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_460,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_461 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "62e110b6e8a592d8c37ad516c7a53772"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The Buddha frequently reminded his followers to keep the Dhamma in mind. He didn't say when to have the Dhamma in mind, but just said to have the Dhamma in mind. Unless we are always meditating, delusion will step in and hold the door open for all the other defilements to move in."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_46 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_1,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_47 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Acknowledgements"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1c0c39fefd100bb3a0bb04acc06d2757"^^xsd:string ;
