    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Daily life will be full of ups and downs when greed, anger, delusion, and all their relatives come on strong. The wisdom you've got may not be sufficient enough to stop them. How do you approach such a situation? The first step is to accept whatever is happening in the mind as it is. Accept that this is just the nature of the mind. Unless you accept, you will be fighting defilements with defilements. I draw the analogy of trying to accelerate a car with one foot on the brakes! The car won't move."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_787 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_23,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_572,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_597,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_788,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_86 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e4c2a3302a982a1a0f3440dcf0722259"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "So, when you begin, the mind may not necessarily completely be open to this process. That's fine. This is how you start when you're developing your meditation skills. Learn from these different situations. Later on, you'll begin to notice causes and effects. Understanding the causes that lead to greater momentum in the practice will allow your meditation to improve naturally."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_789 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_583,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_757,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_790,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_791,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_792 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e0b662042fc16e48fb3c806db9579759"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "While something is happening, awareness will continue to collect data little by little in the background and wisdom will step in when there is enough data. When wisdom steps in, you will no longer continue with the unskillful action. Acknowledge and work through these challenging situations instead of avoiding them. When the mind comes understand that something that is wrong is wrong, it will not repeat an action again. The lessons are all there for you to work through."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_793 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_168,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_18,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_208,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_43,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_531,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_559,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_794,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_795,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_796,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_81 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "dd993865cc5f51b419fc2e4d05eca24c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "What kind of understanding can you glean from what is happening? You can start by being interested. Then investigate. You will become aware of many different things but be mindful that these are just objects or experiences. Begin to ask more questions: What is a concept? What is reality? Continue to watch and learn."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_797 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_223,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_252,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_419,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_45,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_559,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_798,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_799,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_800,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_801 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "51d044417ee6cd154778065e6f74801b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Cultivate curiosity and interest--they are important ingredients. Don't be afraid of making mistakes, and never feel bad about having made a mistake. These false steps are the stepping-stones on our path and a part of our progress. We cannot avoid making them. Becoming aware of, carefully looking at, and learning from mistakes is wisdom at work! As we learn from our mistakes, wisdom will start coming in more naturally, more automatically. Over the years, as our practice progresses, as we become more and more mindful, the knowledge and understanding we have accumulated will naturally come in more quickly. Wisdom and mindfulness will start working as a team."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_8 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_10,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_9 ;
