        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_437,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_44,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_463,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_54,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_558,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_69,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_829 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "HOW TO WORK WITH DIFFICULTIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b273230a2926df6b499cdcfc99bacc84"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "For me, I understood that difficulties would decrease if I practiced mindfulness. I noticed that the intensity of suffering and problems would decrease when I practiced. Truly understanding this motivated me to continue. When real understanding is present and strong, the mind changes for the better. If wisdom isn't strong enough, the mind can't change because defilements still arise. There are people who know about meditation but they don't practice; for these people, their minds do not really change."^^xsd:string .

