    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Reflect. Learn. Keep Going."^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DON'T LET GO OF MINDFULNESS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7c534e3ee1c0097c389a55ecfe258182"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "I became prepared when people came to talk to me. Other people can be full of defilements too and they come and unload their defilements on us. If we are not ready, we get affected and infected. Even with family members, I began to realize that I could not just relax. I could not drop mindfulness. My mindfulness got better and more continuous. This is how we learn from life--our failures and difficulties teach us."^^xsd:string .

