        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_958,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_959,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_960,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_961,
        ex:node_4_2970e5b0_c019_4056_86a0_f3b0ab208a9b_962 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "CAUSES AND CONDITIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5a52aa911dc01103b02bb4726beb39b9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Without awareness + wisdom, the unwholesome mental states can gain momentum unbeknownst to you. When there is knowing, you begin to notice how the habit of anger could arise in the absence of awareness or wisdom and how the process unfolds naturally. It's all about mental processes; it's never about the story or external things. When you understand the benefit of something, the harm of the opposite becomes obvious."^^xsd:string .

