    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "CAUSES AND CONDITIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e7ed444a8565386c7f9b451055336c18"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "I usually tell yogis to stay away from the storyline, but it can help to see the idea that the story carries. The story might be, \"Anne was making a noise and I felt really angry with her\" while the idea behind that might be \"people shouldn't make noise.\" This idea influences the mind. But when it is seen clearly for what it is, that this idea is not helpful, then it can be let go."^^xsd:string .

