    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "RELATING TO OTHERS WISELY"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aa68cdb9d5164f6fa779d777a5c373e4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "So, love as much as you can but do not get attached. What emotions come up when you think about someone you love? If there is only love, there is only happiness. But love can get mixed up with a bit of attachment and that's followed by fear. Loss is a natural part of life so there will be loss eventually. We need to understand it instead of fearing it. Every day we are losing time, losing the object, losing awareness, in every moment."^^xsd:string .

